    "slug": "somalia-s-pm-replaces-defence-minister-in-limited-cabinet-reshuffle",
    "summary": "Prime Minister Hamza Abdi Barre removed Defence Minister Ahmed Moallim Fiqi and appointed lawmaker Saadaq Omar Mohamed Hassan (Saadaq Joon) in his place, a move driven by clan power-sharing after leadership changes in Galmudug state.",
    "content": "Somali Prime Minister Hamza Abdi Barre on Monday dismissed Defence Minister Ahmed Moallim Fiqi and immediately appointed lawmaker Saadaq Omar Mohamed Hassan, commonly known as Saadaq Joon, as his replacement. The change was announced in Mogadishu and takes effect immediately, according to government sources.\n\nThe reshuffle is limited in scope and is attributed to clan power-sharing considerations following recent leadership changes in Galmudug state, rather than any policy disagreement or performance issue. Fiqi, a close ally of President Hassan Sheikh Mohamud and one of the government's most vocal figures, had served as defence minister since April 2025. His removal is seen as part of a political recalibration to maintain balance among Somalia's federal member states and clans.\n\nSaadaq Joon, a former Banadir Regional Administration official and current lawmaker, assumes the defence portfolio at a time when security remains a top priority for the federal government. His appointment is expected to bring a different perspective to the ministry, though specific policy directions have not been outlined.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, the reshuffle signals ongoing political dynamics that could affect security cooperation and reconstruction efforts. Many diaspora members have ties to the defence sector through funding, expertise, or family connections, and changes in leadership may influence how they engage with government initiatives. The move also underscores the importance of clan balance in Somali politics, a factor that often shapes diaspora involvement in national affairs.\n\nThe appointment of Saadaq Joon comes as Somalia continues to navigate complex security challenges, including ongoing operations against al-Shabaab. The international community, including diaspora-funded projects, will be watching how the new minister approaches his role. The government has not indicated any broader cabinet changes at this time.\n\nRead the original report from Somalia Guardian here: https://www.somaliguardian.com/news/somalia-news/somalia-replaces-defence-minister-ahmed-moallim-fiqi-saadaq-omar-mohamed-hassan/",
